; C2, the book's reading  Winning 42 p. 25 (W42-p025-a)
; Reading, in our words: when the partner follows the bidder's trump lead with
; the highest trump the bidder does not hold, the partner has no trump left.
; Written from the bidder's chair, inside the trick, after the partner's play.
; The trigger is the record; the reading is the event "the partner is void in
; trump". Over the bidder's uniform worlds it is a probability, not a fact: it
; holds only of a partner who follows the convention (GAPS.md, policy
; likelihood). "The bidder does not hold" reads the bidder's own hand through
; `holds`, a world predicate: this is a question about worlds, not a policy.
(query
  (roles (chair b) (chair p) (domino led) (domino his))
  (out)
  (pattern
    (viewer b)
    (declarer b)
    (partner b p)
    (leader b)
    (trick-play b led)
    (in led q*)
    (trick-play p his)
    (in his q*)
    (none (roles (domino above)) (live above) (not (holds b above)) (beats above his q*))
    (void p q*)))
